From 9bf33f2c949e9131916ec41a8b7c9e75ee823b9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zinc Lim <zinclim@meta.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:00:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/i2c/aspeed_i2c: only raise the target IRQ for
 enabled sources

aspeed_i2c_bus_raise_slave_interrupt() asserts the bus IRQ whenever
I2CS_INTR_STS is non-zero, without masking against I2CS_INTR_CTRL. Its
master-side counterpart aspeed_i2c_bus_raise_interrupt() has always
masked (raise_irq = sts & intr_ctrl_mask), so we should follow that here.

Master and target share a single output line, and that line is level
triggered: qemu_irq_lower() is reached only from the INTR_STS write
handlers. Asserting for a status bit the guest has masked therefore
creates a request the guest cannot satisfy. Its ISR computes sts & ctrl,
finds nothing it subscribed to, returns IRQ_NONE and consequently never
writes I2CS_INTR_STS, so the line stays high and the CPU re-enters the
handler immediately. Linux counts 100k unhandled interrupts and disables
the line outright:

  irq 50: nobody cared (try booting with the "irqpoll" option)
  Comm: mctpi2c4/tx
   ast2600_i2c_setup_buff_tx from ast2600_i2c_controller_xfer
   ast2600_i2c_controller_xfer from __i2c_transfer
   __i2c_transfer from mctp_i2c_tx_thread
  handlers: [<...>] ast2600_i2c_bus_irq
  Disabling IRQ #50

Once IRQ 50 is gone the bus is dead and every later transfer fails with
-EBUSY:

  i2c i2c-4: __i2c_transfer failed -16

Every target raise is exposed to this, including the DMA mode I2C_FINISH
path that has been there since target support was added. Buffer mode RX
just makes it easy to hit, because it raises mid-transfer each time the
pool needs re-arming rather than only at STOP.

Mask the raise against I2CS_INTR_CTRL. Status bits still latch while
masked; they simply do not drive the line. Since suppressing the raise
would otherwise lose an interrupt that the guest enables later, also
re-evaluate pending target status on writes to I2CS_INTR_CTRL, matching
how a real controller asserts on unmask.

Signed-off-by: Zinc Lim <zinclim@meta.com>
---
 hw/i2c/aspeed_i2c.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/i2c/aspeed_i2c.c b/hw/i2c/aspeed_i2c.c
index f82775a210..8288e6c7f3 100644
--- a/hw/i2c/aspeed_i2c.c
+++ b/hw/i2c/aspeed_i2c.c
@@ -83,8 +83,10 @@ static inline void aspeed_i2c_bus_raise_interrupt(AspeedI2CBus *bus)
 static inline void aspeed_i2c_bus_raise_slave_interrupt(AspeedI2CBus *bus)
 {
     AspeedI2CClass *aic = ASPEED_I2C_GET_CLASS(bus->controller);
+    uint32_t sts = bus->regs[R_I2CS_INTR_STS];
+    uint32_t ctrl = bus->regs[R_I2CS_INTR_CTRL];
 
-    if (!bus->regs[R_I2CS_INTR_STS]) {
+    if (!(sts & ctrl)) {
         return;
     }
 
@@ -901,6 +903,7 @@ static void aspeed_i2c_bus_new_write(AspeedI2CBus *bus, hwaddr offset,
         break;
     case A_I2CS_INTR_CTRL:
         bus->regs[R_I2CS_INTR_CTRL] = value;
+        aspeed_i2c_bus_raise_slave_interrupt(bus);
         break;
 
     case A_I2CS_INTR_STS:
